# App loading contract

Keep the page inventory in `packages/onsocial-app/src/lib/app-loading-matrix.ts`
up to date when adding or changing a page.

## State behavior

- Cold with no painted data → structural skeleton matching the final shell.
- Refresh with painted data → keep rows; use a refresh treatment.
- Load more → append skeleton rows; never replace painted rows.
- Empty or cold error → in-flow state.
- Error with painted rows → `OsChromeListAlert` / whisper overlay.
- Intermittent chrome → fixed overlay or `null`; never reserve hidden flow.

## Geometry

- Skeleton and production rows share layout primitives, variants, and tokens.
- Route `loading.tsx` must preserve the page shell when the shell is known.
- `Suspense fallback={null}` is only valid when an already-mounted shell remains
  visible and a blank first navigation is not possible.
- New content requires updating the real layout, skeleton, matrix row, and
  contract/visual coverage together.
